@@ -55,3 +55,11 @@ Playwright checks Chromium's accessibility tree through a complete keyboard jour
 Tree record: Chromium 156.0.8078.4 and Playwright 1.64.1. Screen reader: not run. Spoken journey: user acceptance.
 
 Delivered projects from document setups keep the product specification in `docs/`.
+
+## Tournament
+
+Tournament, beside New Game, runs a knockout for 4 or 8 people on one device. Enter names in seed order, then choose Start tournament. Each player selects Start turn and plays the same board code as their opponent. Select Next turn or Next match to hand over the device. Quarterfinals use 4x4, semifinals 6x6 and the final 8x8. Lower moves wins, then lower active time, then the higher seed (seed 1 is highest). The existing clock starts at the first card reveal and excludes time while the page is hidden or a leave dialog is open.
+
+Tournament boards leave your saved grid size and best scores unchanged. Leave tournament asks before discarding unfinished work. Completed brackets show the champion and remain in Past tournaments after reload. The newest ten records use `np3:tournaments`; blocked storage keeps records in memory for this page session and displays a notice.
+
+Every tournament screen has a Tournament JSON box with Export tournament and Load tournament. Exports use `neon-pairs/tournament`, version 3, and include names, board codes, results and any active game snapshot. A loaded active turn continues its saved progress. Loading over unfinished work asks first. Names are normalized and checked on entry and import; invalid files leave play unchanged. Existing snapshot and preference formats keep their version and keys.
